Package: gulogulo
Version: @VERSION@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Sythos <sythos@gmail.com>
Depends: systemd
Homepage: https://github.com/Sythos/GuloGulo
Description: Gulo Gulo groupware runtime (mail, calendar, contacts)
 Gulo Gulo is a self-hosted, tenant-isolated groupware runtime (mail,
 calendar, contacts) built on a single TypeScript application core. This
 package installs it to /opt/gulogulo and runs it as a dedicated systemd
 service (gulogulo.service) under its own system user, behind a reverse
 proxy you configure yourself - postinst writes a reviewable nginx example
 to /opt/gulogulo/gulogulo-proxy.conf.example but never applies it.
 .
 Requires Node.js >= 26 already installed and on PATH before this package
 is configured; postinst checks this and aborts configuration if it is
 missing or too old. This is deliberately not declared as an apt Depends:
 no Debian Trixie main-archive or independently verified NodeSource apt
 repository providing Node.js 26 on Trixie was confirmed as reliable at
 packaging time - see INSTALL.md for how to install Node.js 26 first
 (NodeSource's setup_26.x script) before installing this package.
 .
 PostgreSQL is optional and configured via /opt/gulogulo/.env after
 install; this package does not depend on or install a database server.
 .
 No native/compiled dependencies are bundled - the application uses only
 pure-JavaScript/TypeScript npm packages (ldapts, pg) and Node's built-in
 crypto module for password hashing (scrypt), which is why this package is
 Architecture: all rather than architecture-specific.
